      "description": "Answer options in the classifier, stacked in one ruled box.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-sel\" role=\"radiogroup\"><button role=\"radio\" aria-checked=\"true\" class=\"ds-on\"><span class=\"ds-r\"><span></span></span>Lateral only<kbd>1</kbd></button><button role=\"radio\" aria-checked=\"false\"><span class=\"ds-r\"></span>Bimalleolar<kbd>2</kbd></button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-sel{width:360px;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:4px;background:var(--card)}.ds-sel button{display:flex;width:100%;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:12px 16px;border:0;border-top:1px solid var(--border);background:none;color:var(--foreground);font:500 14px Archivo,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;text-align:left;transition:background-color .15s}.ds-sel button:first-child{border-top:0}.ds-sel button:hover{background:var(--muted)}.ds-sel button.ds-on{background:var(--accent);color:var(--accent-foreground)}.ds-sel button:focus-visible{outline:none;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px var(--ring)}.ds-r{display:flex;width:16px;height:16px;align-items:center;justify-content:center;border:1px solid var(--input);border-radius:9999px}.ds-on .ds-r{border-color:var(--primary)}.ds-r span{width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:9999px;background:var(--primary)}.ds-sel kbd{margin-left:auto;min-width:20px;height:20px;padding:0 6px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--muted);color:var(--muted-foreground);font:500 11px/20px Archivo,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;text-align:center}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Classification Chart",
    "overview": "Anklyze looks like a printed clinical reference chart: navy ink on white paper, every group of facts held in a box drawn with a 1px rule, and the classification codes set large and heavy where the eye lands first. Depth comes from rules and tonal fills, never from shadows, gradients, glow or glass. The interface is dense and quiet so the radiograph and the result carry the page.\n\nThere is one typeface, Archivo, self-hosted as a variable font. Its narrow, heavy cut is the display voice for headlines and classification codes; its normal width carries everything else. Copy is sentence case throughout. Colour is reserved: navy is the only accent, and four identity hues mark the four classification systems and nothing else.\n\nResults and reliability figures are printed for papers and case notes, so print is a supported medium: chrome drops out and the page prints black on white.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Navy ink on near-white; a solid navy field is the only saturated surface.",
      "1px rules group content; ruled grids instead of floating cards.",
      "Flat at rest; state shows as a tonal fill or a 2px rule, not a lift.",
      "One typeface in two voices: narrow heavy display, normal-width body.",
      "Small radii (0 to 4px); square swatches and badges.",
      "Exact numbers in tabular figures, with their method stated beside them."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Identity Colour Rule",
        "body": "The four system hues identify a classification system and are used for nothing else: no status, no decoration, no emphasis.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Field Rule",
        "body": "Field Navy is the only saturated surface, used as one full-bleed band on a public page. App pages stay on Paper.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flag, Not Paint Rule",
        "body": "Status colour marks an exception (a low value, a missing CT) or a lifecycle dot. Ordinary values are never coloured.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "Display voice is for headlines and codes only; everything else is normal-width Archivo. Monospace is limited to text meant to be copied verbatim.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Exact Figure Rule",
        "body": "Tables and anything marked `data-numeric` use tabular figures. Percentages print with one decimal.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ruled Box Rule",
        "body": "Group facts in a box drawn with a 1px rule; split it into cells with `gap-px` over a Rule-coloured background or with `divide-y`, not with separate floating cards.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do open every app page with PageHeader and group content in boxes drawn with a 1px rule.",
      "Do mark a classification system with its identity swatch and its proper name (Lauge-Hansen, Danis-Weber, AO/OTA, Bartonicek), which is never translated, in that display order.",
      "Do set classification codes and published figures in the display voice with tabular figures, and place a MethodNote beside reliability figures.",
      "Do show \"not classifiable\" as a muted result, never as an error.",
      "Do write sentence case, keep all strings in `frontend/src/i18n/{en,es}.json`, and address the reader as usted in Spanish (\"Seleccione\", \"Introduzca\", \"Inicie sesión\").",
      "Do ship every screen in both themes and keep print legible."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use shadows, gradients, glows or glass on resting surfaces.",
      "Don't use a system identity hue for status, emphasis or decoration.",
      "Don't colour a normal value; status colour flags exceptions only.",
      "Don't add a second display or text typeface, or use the display voice for body copy.",
      "Don't use uppercase eyebrows or letter-spaced labels.",
      "Don't animate entrances with slides or scales; content swaps fade."
    ]
